    "wordpress",
    "misconfiguration",
    "data-exposure",
    "backup-exposure",
    "operations",
    "local-play",
    "container",
    "multi-verify"
  ],
  "exposedPorts": [
    {
      "port": 18080,
      "name": "Web (WordPress site)"
    },
    {
      "port": 18081,
      "name": "/verify (loopback admin)"
    }
  ],
  "learningGoals": [
    "WordPress は PHP・DB・認証・設定の上で動いていて、 デフォルトや初期設定を放置すると何が守れなくなるかを、 実際の環境で体感できるようになる",
    "バックアップ・設定ファイルの控え・デバッグログ・ディレクトリ一覧など、 別々の運用不備が同じ 「公開領域への置き忘れ」 から生まれることを、 自分で確かめられるようになる",
    "公開領域に置くファイルの見直し・不要ファイルの削除・ディレクトリ一覧の無効化・デバッグ出力の停止が、 コードを触らずにできる基本の対策であることを理解する"
  ],
  "i18n": {
    "en": {
      "writeup": "Fixture wp-exposed-backup: .i18n.en.writeup. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "name": "The Predecessor's Leftovers",
      "shortDescription": "Fixture wp-exposed-backup: .i18n.en.shortDescription. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "instructions": "Fixture wp-exposed-backup: .i18n.en.instructions. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "description": "Fixture wp-exposed-backup: .i18n.en.description. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "learningGoals": [
        "Feel, in a real environment, that WordPress runs on PHP, a DB, auth, and settings — and what stops being protected when defaults and initial setup are left alone",
        "Confirm, yourself, that separate operational mistakes — a backup, a config copy, a debug log, a directory listing — all grow from the same 'left it in the public area' habit",
        "Understand that reviewing what goes in public folders, deleting unneeded files, turning off directory listing, and stopping debug output are the basic, code-free fixes"
      ],
